Electrical protection 

Our datacenter, has its own EDF transformer (20KV-1MKVA) integrated into a redundant EDF (Électricité de France) loop, thus ensuring optimal management of operations and maintenance. This transformer is installed in a secure room within the building. 

The main low-voltage switchboard, dedicated to power distribution within the building, is located in a secure area adjacent to the transformer. An auxiliary low-voltage panel ensures the site’s specific power supply and manages the switch to backup power if needed. 

Power generator, providing 48 hours of autonomy at full load (700 liters of fuel plus 2,000 liters in reserve tanks), ensures uninterrupted service in the event of a failure by the electricity supplier. Its fuel supply can be maintained during operation. The entire power switching chain is subject to monthly real-life scenario testing. 

The generator, which undergoes monthly maintenance, is positioned on the roof in a secure area, and its technical alarms are connected both to the building’s alarm system and to remote monitoring. 

 

The inverter section benefits from power module redundancy with a minimum 2N configuration, along with continuous monitoring of critical indicators (load levels, autonomy, etc.) to ensure alerts in the event of an incident. A dedicated inverter distribution panel provides redundant power supply to racks and servers via two separate lines, each feeding a 32A three-phase 10 KVA PDU rail. 

