Air conditioning 

Zone de texte 11, Zone de texteThe hosting room is equipped with a high-capacity system, sized according to the available electrical power. To optimize server cooling, a “Cold-Corridor” containment solution was selected: cold air is blown into the raised technical flooring, then rises into an isolated cold aisle to efficiently cool the equipment. The expelled hot air then circulates through the ambient air of the datacenter before returning to the air conditioning units. This system limits the amount of flammable materials, improves the energy efficiency of air conditioning, and allows for greater thermal density within the racks. The air conditioning systems are of the "direct expansion" type, equipped with its own rooftop air condenser, located in the secure technical area of the building, as well as its own refrigeration circuit. An annual maintenance contract and a 24/7/365 intervention contract are in place to ensure optimal operation. These systems also regulate the humidity levels within the data center. 

Supervision 

The monitoring and supervision console ensures continuous surveillance of the datacenter infrastructure. All systems (temperature, humidity levels, access control, and power consumption) as well as servers (CPU, RAM, storage, etc.) are monitored in real time. In the event of an incident, alerts are sent to the data center service at any time of day or night. 

Fire safety 

The hosting room is equipped with an automated early smoke detection system, covering both the ambient space and the raised floor. This system relies on multi-point detectors capable of identifying the onset of a fire or the abnormal presence of combustion products by analyzing the atmospheric composition. 

A dedicated device monitors the air circulating beneath the raised floor, while another oversees the overall environment of the data center. If an anomaly is detected, technical and on-call teams are immediately informed via the central alarm and remote monitoring system. 

If the central system confirms the presence of a fire, the automatic extinguishing procedure is triggered. Suppression is carried out by nitrogen cylinders, which reduce the oxygen concentration in the data center air to below 11%. The room’s airtightness maintains this level for the duration required for intervention by specialized teams. 

The entire system is covered by a maintenance and intervention contract. The maintenance schedule is as follows: 

Detection and suppression system maintenance: semi-annual. 

Venti-Test to verify room airtightness : annual 

For your information, a full-scale test of the detection and suppression devices was conducted successfully in 2010, prior to the room’s commissioning, to ensure compliance and the effectiveness of the fire safety systems. 

