Internet connectivity 

AVA6 works with several operators (Colt, Orange, Jaguar, Ntt, Hopus, Cogent, Acorus, Hurricane) to provide high-quality national and international peering. Our Internet access is protected by an Anti-DDOS system, with redundant internal router management, BGP, and ownership of our public IPv4 and IPv6 addresses. The fiber connections are redundant, with dual entry points, and a 2-hour MTTR according to our contracts, with delivery at different points of our backbone to guarantee service continuity. 

Our server centers are connected to multiple interconnection nodes (GIX), notably LyonIX I and II. As part of a Disaster Recovery Plan (BRP), interconnection with LyonIX has enabled the implementation of a backbone featuring a high-capacity (Gbps) loop and enhanced security through dual fiber, which also allows for the deployment of the Business Continuity Plan (BCP). These GIX facilitate direct interconnections with companies present at these nodes and can improve migration to AVA6 Datacenters in this context. This infrastructure ensures a fiber connection between the Villeurbanne Datacenter and LyonIX II. The security of this link is further strengthened thanks to a redundant (Backbone) loop. 

